.Dd November 12, 2026
.Dt SSH3 1
.Os ssh3-rust
.Sh NAME
.Nm ssh3
.Nd SSH3 client: sessions, forwards and file transfers over HTTP/3
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl 46AfMNqTvVtT
.Op Fl i Ar identity_file
.Op Fl p Ar port
.Op Fl U Ar url_path
.Op Fl L Ar [bind_address:]port:host:hostport
.Op Fl R Ar [bind_address:]bind_port Ns Op /udp Ns :target_host:target_port
.Op Fl D Ar [bind_address:]port
.Op Fl J Ar destination
.Op Fl o Ar key=value
.Op Fl S Ar ctl_path
.Op Fl O Ar op
.Op Fl F Ar ssh_config
.Op Fl s Ar subsystem
.Ar [user@]host Ns Op :port
.Op Ar command ...
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
connects to an
.Xr ssh3-rust-server 8
endpoint: one QUIC
.Pq UDP
connection carries an HTTP/3 extended CONNECT
.Rs
.%T RFC 9220
.%D October 2022
.Re
to the secret server route
.Pq the Fl U Ar url_path ,
default
.Li /ssh3-term ,
and every subsequent bidirectional stream is an SSH3 channel for
sessions, forwards and file transfers.
The launch flags follow the
.Xr ssh 1
canon, and the
.Fl o
keywords accept the OpenSSH shapes; the precedence is the CLI flag, then
the
.Fl o
keyword, then
.Pa ~/.ssh/config .
.Pp
Authentication: the public keys of the identity files
.Pq Fl i
and of the authentication plugins, the agent
.Pq Fl -agent ,
the OIDC flow
.Pq Fl -use-oidc ,
a bearer token
.Pq Fl -bearer-token-file ,
or the Basic password step
.Pq Fl -password-file .
The first connection pins the server certificate in
.Pa ~/.ssh3/known_hosts
(trust on first use); the
.Fl -strict-host-key-checking
policy
.Pq and the StrictHostKeyChecking -o keyword ,
.Cm ask
by default, governs the pin/ask/refuse decision afterwards.
.Pp
The transfer mode
.Pq Fl -transfer
is the scp analog: exactly one operand is a local path, the other is
.Ar user@host:remote_path
.Ns — the remote side decides the direction, the explicit form
.Ar user@host:port/url_path:remote_path
carries the server addressing as well.
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl 4 , Fl 6
Force the IPv4/IPv6 address family for the QUIC dial.
.It Fl i Ar identity_file
The private key file for public key authentication; the
.Fl -privkey
spelling is the deprecated alias of the reference.
.It Fl -server-name Ar name
The TLS server name the certificate is validated against, when it
differs from the host of the URL.
.It Fl -user Ar name
The user the session requests; the
.Fl o Cm User
keyword and
.Ev USER
carry the same value.
.It Fl -agent , Fl -agent-key Ar path , Fl -agent-socket Ar path
Authenticate through the OpenSSH agent: the whole agent, one of its
keys, or the agent at the given socket
.Pq the Ev SSH_AUTH_SOCK default .
.It Fl A , Fl -forward-agent
Forward the ssh agent to the remote host.
.It Fl -password Ar pass , Fl -password-file Ar path
The Basic authentication password; the file form keeps the secret out
of the argument list.
.It Fl -bearer-token Ar token , Fl -bearer-token-file Ar path
The bearer token sent in the Authorization header.
.It Fl -use-oidc Ar issuer , Fl -oidc-client-id Ar id , Fl -oidc-client-secret Ar secret , Fl -oidc-client-secret-file Ar path , Fl -oidc-config Ar path , Fl -no-pkce
The OIDC flow: the issuer URL, the client credentials and their JSON
config file
.Pq the reference name Pa ~/.ssh3/oidc_config.json ,
the PKCE switch.
.It Fl -keylog Ar file
Write the QUIC TLS secrets in the NSS keylog format; only for
debugging with a packet analyzer.
.It Fl -ca-cert Ar path , Fl -insecure
The extra root certificates; the insecure switch turns the
certificate verification off.
.It Fl -strict-host-key-checking Cm ask | yes | accept-new | no
The policy of the known_hosts check
.Pq default Cm ask .
.It Fl -known-hosts Ar path
The known_hosts file that pins the server certificates
.Pq default Pa ~/.ssh3/known_hosts .
.It Fl -transfer , Fl r , Fl -continue , Fl -checksum
The file transfer mode and its modifiers: the recursive trees, the
resumption of an interrupted transfer, and the SHA-256 verification
(automatic over 32 MiB).
.It Fl p Ar port , Fl U Ar url_path
The port and the secret route of the server.
.It Fl t , Fl T
Force, never allocate a pseudo-terminal; the
.Fl o Cm RequestTTY
keyword carries the
.Cm auto | yes | no | force
shapes.
.It Fl o Ar key=value
Configuration option, repeatable: Cm RequestTTY, Term, EscapeChar,
StrictHostKeyChecking, LocalForward, RemoteForward, DynamicForward,
ProxyJump, ServerAliveInterval .
.It Fl L Ar [bind_address:]port:host:hostport
Local forwarding towards the remote host; the
.Fl -forward-tcp
and
.Fl -forward-udp
spellings are the deprecated aliases of the reference.
.It Fl R Ar [bind_address:]bind_port Ns Op /udp Ns :target_host:target_port
Reverse forwarding: the server binds and forwards to the local target.
.It Fl D Ar [bind_address:]port
Dynamic (SOCKS5) forwarding.
.It Fl J Ar destination
Proxy jump: a comma-separated chain of SSH3 hops, tunneled hop by hop;
the
.Fl -proxy-jump
spelling is the deprecated alias.
.It Fl N
No remote command or session: hold the connection open for the
forwards.
.It Fl f
Go to background after the startup checks: the session detaches from
the terminal and keeps running.
.It Fl M , Fl S Ar ctl_path , Fl O Cm check | stop | exit , Fl -control-master Cm no | yes | auto , Fl -control-path Ar path , Fl -control-persist Cm no | yes | Ns Ar seconds
The control master: share one authenticated connection across the
invocations through the unix socket
.Ar ctl_path ,
its operations and the idle persistence.
.It Fl F Ar ssh_config
The ssh_config file to read instead of
.Pa ~/.ssh/config .
.It Fl s Ar subsystem
Request the subsystem on the session channel instead of a shell;
.Cm sftp
launches the built-in interactive SFTP client.
.It Fl -handshake-idle-timeout Ar duration , Fl -max-idle-timeout Ar duration , Fl -packet-size Ar bytes
The QUIC tuning: the handshake and idle timeouts, the initial packet
size.
.It Fl q , Fl v
Quiet / verbose diagnostics; the
.Ev SSH3_LOG_LEVEL
of the reference folds onto the same ladder.
.It Fl V
Print the version string and exit.
.El
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Ev SSH3_LOG_LEVEL
The diagnostic level of the reference
.Pq Cm trace | debug | info | warning | error .
The names fold onto the client levels by severity: error and warning
quiet the client, info carries the ordinary level, debug and trace add
the details. The exact lowercase
.Cm trace
spelling beats the
.Fl q
and
.Fl v
flags, every other name yields to them; an unknown name keeps the
ordinary default.
.It Ev SSH_AUTH_SOCK
The socket of the OpenSSH agent, the default of
.Fl -agent-socket .
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Pa ~/.ssh3/known_hosts
The TOFU pin store of the server certificates.
.It Pa ~/.ssh/config
The OpenSSH configuration, consulted by default for the implemented
keywords;
.Fl F
reads another file.
.It Pa ~/.ssh3/oidc_config.json
The reference name of the OIDC JSON client config.
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr ssh3-rust-server 8 ,
.Xr ssh 1 ,
.Xr ssh_config 5
